  "body": "## What changed\n\nThis PR adds regression coverage for the 2D corner check on a bore drawn as chords.\nThe test calls `unreached_corners` and `unreached_corner_note` with three generated bores.\nIt checks that micron-sized cusps do not stop the check or produce a corner note.\n\nThe production fix is already on main in `bc5daa32d` (`outer_fills`).\nThe remaining diff adds the chord-bore test and `docs/decisions/2849-corner-cusp-loop.md`.\nMain's bow-tie test checks `outer_fills` directly. This test covers both corner-check entry points.\n\nThis is partial work for #2849. The other defects on that issue remain open.\n\n## Pin and mutation check\n\nPin: `machining2d::unreached::law::a_chord_cusp_that_crosses_itself_does_not_stop_the_corner_check` (`camcraft-motion`, lib).\n\n- The test builds 25 mm bores with 50, 60 and 63 chords.\n- It uses reach values of 2, 3 and 4 mm.\n- It asserts that both calls succeed, find no corner and return no note.\n- Mutation check: replacing `Region::from_slices` with `Region::new` in `outer_fills` makes the pin fail with `loop crosses itself`.\n- Restoring the exact original source makes the pin pass: 1 passed, 0 failed. The mutation was not committed.\n\n## Gate results\n\nHead: `c01305462e0a169caf4d6b210226a8debfb57e89`.\nBase: `upstream/main` at `60cb97a0b3717bf6a129e781fd8f4ec98806124b`.\n\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main`: green. The full run completed all 236 steps in 44.2 minutes.\n- The run reached every motion and app heavy target: 100 tests passed. Six tracked known failures failed as expected.\n- Motion: 57 passed and 2 expected failures. App: 43 passed and 4 expected failures.\n- The gate reported zero failed steps. It classified each tracked known failure as an expected result.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green. Both steps passed in 3.8 minutes.\n- Motion lib: 491 passed, 10 ignored. App `adaptive_zero_margin_island`: 4 passed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean in 57.18 seconds.\n\n\n### Heavy lanes that ran\n\nThe counts below are passing tests in each nonempty target. All other selected targets ran with zero ignored tests.\n\n- `motion heavy`: `lib` (8), `adaptive_hsm` (5), `adaptive_troch_neck` (1), `finish3d` (33), `finish3d_gaplink` (1), `flow` (2), `lead_room` (1), `offset_shells` (1), `pivot5d` (1), `pocket3d_hsm` (1), `rotary_adaptive` (3).\n- `app heavy`: `adaptive_fig8_crossing` (2), `adaptive_pinch` (1), `carried_engine_agreement` (1), `example_catalog` (2), `feature_pick_wire` (1), `import_solidcraft` (3), `large_models` (1), `lathe_field_sim` (1), `lathe_workholding_kinds` (1), `operations` (6), `pick_agnostic` (2), `pocket3d_hsm` (1), `rotary_field_parity` (6), `shared_face_bodies_finish` (6), `shoulder_adaptive` (1), `stock_engine_agreement` (3), `stock_field_cost` (1), `stock_play_precalc` (1), `verify` (2), `whole_model_pocket` (1).\n\nThe following tracked known failures ran and failed as expected. Their defects remain open.\nThe #2849 tests import `Milling-test.step` through `ImportModel` with the fine solidcore mesh.\n\n- #1950: `machining2d::pocket_hsm::ring_tests::the_stock_ring_level_reaches_the_air_planner_with_the_stock` (`motion`, lib).\n- #1950: `machining2d::pocket_hsm::ring_tests::the_stock_ring_level_plans_adaptive_with_no_budget_note` (`motion`, lib).\n- #1950: `the_users_whole_model_bore_roughs_adaptive_on_each_level` (`app`, `pocket3d_hsm`).\n- #2849: `an_axis_aligned_lead_start_posts_the_users_arc_entry_as_g18_or_g19` (`app`, `lead_approach`).\n- #2849: `the_horizontal_arc_entry_on_the_users_pocket_verifies_silent` (`app`, `lead_approach`).\n- #2849: `fig8_outside_containment_with_em0800_and_clearing_kinds_works` (`app`, `shoulder_adaptive`).\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- An interactive GUI reproduction. The tests exercise generated bores and the imported `Milling-test.step` model.\n\nChangelog: Add regression coverage for the 2D corner check on bores whose chord cusps cross themselves.\n\nEffort: high\n\nRefs #2849\n",
